# .dockerignore -- bifrost-router MINIMAL BUILD CONTEXT
# Context root: the bifrost-router repo root.
#   ORIGINAL   f9bffce, 578 files, 19,636,069 B -> 67 files / 1,777,868 B reached the build.
#   2026-10-15 the capture moved to f5e6ca3 (591 files) and this list was RECHECKED by
#              recomputing the import closure of main:app with an AST walk over the new
#              tree. Exactly one module was missing: airgap.py, which autopilot_graph.py,
#              strategies.py and subtask_graph.py all import and which did not exist at
#              f9bffce. It is admitted below. Closure is now 41 root modules.
#              The byte/file totals above are from the ORIGINAL measurement and have not
#              been re-measured; treat them as historical, not current.
#   NOTE       a module missing from this list does NOT fail the build. It fails at import
#              or first use, and /health can still answer 200. Re-run the closure check
#              after EVERY re-capture -- a green build is not evidence this list is right.
# Result:       67 files / 1,777,868 B reach the build (was 119 files / 2,180,739 B).
#               67 = 1 requirements + 39 closure modules + 1 ast-read + 6 backends
#                    + 4 runtime JSON + 16 skills.
#               Verified with the repo's OWN matcher -- see "VERIFIED HOW" below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO SYNTAX RULES THIS FILE OBEYS, BOTH LEARNED THE HARD WAY DURING STAGING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. NO TRAILING COMMENTS ON A PATTERN LINE. A '#' is a comment only at the START of a
#    line. A first draft of this file wrote
#        !fleet_config.json              # config.py:178
#    which is the single pattern "fleet_config.json<spaces>#<spaces>config.py:178" and
#    matches nothing. The four runtime JSON files were therefore SILENTLY EXCLUDED, and the
#    image would have started and then died at import on config.py:178. Every annotation in
#    this file is on its own comment line for that reason. Do not "tidy" them back inline.
# 2. NO BARE DIRECTORY RE-INCLUDES. A first draft wrote '!backends', which re-includes the
#    WHOLE directory and silently pulled in backends/block2_4_opener.py -- dev scratch that
#    sits inside the package dir and is in no import path. Re-include per FILE, except
#    skills/ where '!skills/**' is used deliberately (a bare '!skills' does not match
#    anything beneath it; '!skills/**' does, confirmed against the matcher).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY A DENY-ALL FLOOR AND NOT MORE SUBTRACTION PATTERNS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pre-existing bifrost-router/.dockerignore is 190 lines of subtraction over 'COPY . .'.
# Its own 2026-09-04 (K-4) note records that against the running v410 image **63 backup
# files shipped and zero were excluded**, for three reasons, one of which is "the pattern
# LOOKS right": in .dockerignore '*' does not cross '/', so a bare '*.bak-*' is root-only.
# That note names the fix taken here:
#   "a pure `*`-floor whitelist is the ideal end-state -- deferred to the frozen rebuild
#    where the minimal include-set can be smoke-tested"
# This file IS that '*'-floor whitelist. The include-set is not guessed: it is the transitive
# local-import closure of the uvicorn entrypoint main:app, computed with ast.parse over
# BYTES, plus the non-import runtime reads found by auditing every '__file__'-relative path
# in that closure.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE FILE A PURE IMPORT CLOSURE GETS WRONG -- READ BEFORE EDITING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# bifrost_delegate.py is imported by NOTHING in the closure. It is read off disk and parsed
# with ast by igor_tool_loop.py:1017:
#     _SAFE_LEAVES_SRC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),
#                                     "bifrost_delegate.py")
# Its own comment (igor_tool_loop.py:1013-1016) says why it is read and not imported, and
# that "The Router image ships it at /app/bifrost_delegate.py (Dockerfile COPY . .)".
# Drop it from the context and the SAFE_LEAVES table cannot be read, so the tool loop logs
# "refusing every leaf (fail-closed)" (igor_tool_loop.py:1547). The image still STARTS,
# /health still returns 200, and every delegated leaf is refused. That is a guard firing on
# every input -- the exact failure a minimal context introduces and a health check misses.
# ==> THE ACCEPTANCE TEST FOR THIS CONTEXT MUST EXERCISE ONE DELEGATED LEAF.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERIFIED HOW (not asserted)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checked by importing dirtycheck.py from this repo -- the matcher build.ps1 already trusts
# to decide the -dirty stamp (19 tests, tests/test_dirtycheck.py) -- and running
# excluded_from_image() over all 578 paths with these patterns. Result: the 67 files below
# reach the image and 511 do not. Positive assertions (must reach) and negative assertions
# (must not) both pass; the five failures an earlier draft produced are what found the two
# syntax rules at the top of this file.
# Compatibility note: this file does not break the -dirty gate. Under dirtycheck's rule a
# file is excluded iff a non-negated pattern matches it or an ancestor AND no '!' matches
# any of them, so the floor makes the gate MORE exact: only these 67 files can now make the
# tree dirty. Re-run dirtycheck.py and its test module after adopting this file.
# BuildKit is the final authority on the real context. Confirm with the command in
# BUILD-STAGING-2026-10-05.md, which lists the context BuildKit actually sends.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny everything, then allow by name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# ---- deps manifest --------------------------------------------------------
!requirements.txt

# ---- the 39 root modules in the import closure of main:app ----------------
!main.py
!anthropic_compat.py
!anthropic_passthrough.py
!airgap.py
!autopilot_graph.py
!autopilot_state.py
!bifrost_halt.py
!bifrost_message.py
!capability_registry.py
!classifier.py
!commands.py
!config.py
!content_fetch.py
!context_overflow.py
!degenerate.py
!egress_guard.py
!embed_similarity.py
!fetch_guard.py
!free_tier_budget.py
!igor_prompt.py
!igor_tool_loop.py
!langfuse_client.py
!metrics.py
!npu_classifier.py
!npu_classifier_shadow.py
!npu_gate.py
!overlay_dispatch.py
!policy_instructions.py
!pr_review.py
!rag_inject_chromadb.py
!reasoning_coalesce.py
!review_prompts.py
!routing_cache.py
!routing_cache_serve_path.py
!search_query.py
!shadow_embed_guard.py
!startup_checks.py
!strategies.py
!subtask_graph.py
!telemetry.py

# ---- read-with-ast, NOT imported. See the block above before removing. ----
!bifrost_delegate.py

# ---- the backends package: 6 of its 7 files, re-included PER FILE --------
# The 7th, backends/block2_4_opener.py, is dev scratch inside the package dir and is in
# no import path. A bare '!backends' would pull it in; per-file re-includes do not.
!backends/__init__.py
!backends/_retry.py
!backends/anthropic.py
!backends/n8n.py
!backends/ollama.py
!backends/openai_compat.py

# ---- runtime data files, read by path at import time ---------------------
# fleet_config.json           opened by config.py:178            _FLEET_CONFIG_PATH
# capability_registry.json    opened by capability_registry.py:26 _REGISTRY_PATH
# capability_profiles.json    opened by embed_similarity.py:41   _PROFILES_PATH
# bifrost_shell_policy.json   opened by policy_instructions.py:48 _DEFAULT_POLICY_PATH
# (annotations deliberately on their own lines -- see syntax rule 1)
!fleet_config.json
!capability_registry.json
!capability_profiles.json
!bifrost_shell_policy.json

# ---- skill registry, baked at build time per v114.10 PROGRESSIVE-SKILLS-1 -
# 16 files. '!skills/**' is required; a bare '!skills' matches nothing beneath it.
# The pre-existing .dockerignore ends with a "KNOWN AND LEFT ALONE" note about
# skills/router/SKILL.md.bak-ps1-20260519-200928 still shipping. In THIS committed tree
# that file does not exist (find skills -type f => 16 files, no .bak), and the deny-all
# floor makes the note moot either way.
!skills/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IN THE CONTEXT -- each with its reason, so none is a silent drop
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# executors.json            No module in the closure -- or anywhere in the repo outside
#                           patch/scratch files -- opens it. It is config for a consumer
#                           that is not this image. Verified by name grep over all 578
#                           files, with a known positive (fleet_config.json -> config.py).
# decisions.md              autopilot_graph.py:3968 prefers the mounted logs dir and only
#                           falls back to /app/decisions.md. Its own comment says
#                           "__file__.parent is /app -- unmounted, so a decisions.md there
#                           was ephemeral". The live Deployment mounts logs, so baking it
#                           bakes a file that is never read. If a deployment WITHOUT the
#                           logs mount is ever wanted, re-include it and say so.
# backends/block2_4_opener.py  dev scratch inside the package dir; in no import path.
# bifrost_shell.py          The MCP tool surface -- host paths, LAN endpoints, kubectl.
# bifrost_gates.py          Built into SEPARATE images by Dockerfile.bifrost-shell-mcp*.
# bifrost-gates.toml        Nothing in main:app's closure imports them (bifrost_halt.py
# bifrost_shell_static.py   mentions bifrost_gates.py only in a prose comment -- grep
# requirements-mcp.txt      verified line by line, not pattern-matched).
# router_graph.py           Referenced only by a prose comment in backends/ollama.py:31
#                           and by patch_*/fix_* scratch scripts. Not imported.
# preflight.py              The two "preflight" hits in main.py / config.py are CORS
#                           preflight handlers and one comment -- NOT this module. Read
#                           line by line. preflight.py is a BUILD-TIME gate run by
#                           build.ps1 before docker build; it must not be in the image.
# sandbox/                  k8s sandbox tooling, not the router process.
# bfg-1.14.0.jar            14 MB. Shipped into live-v214 by 'COPY . .'.
# BifrostPortal.jsx         134,939 B of portal source. Belongs to the portal unit.
# tests/ evals/ k8s/ dispatch-journal/ phase2/ patches/ scratchpad/ modelfiles/ models/
# rawmark/ reports/ rfp-outputs/ backups/ _readtest/ verify_gates/ .claude/ .github/
# systemd/ mcp-catalog/ plans/ scripts/ tools/        ops + history, 511 files in all.
# Dockerfile* docker-compose* *.ps1 *.bat *.jsx *.jar *.log *.jsonl *.csv *_results.json
# *.pre-* *.bak* *_backup *-preimage-*    backups and superseded snapshots.
